// Title: nontail_result_as_fold_init passes whatever the recursion produces
// Command: graphix-fuzz run tests-functions-fold-init-vacuous.gx
// Expected (if the fixture pinned its subject): a recursion that bottoms
//   makes the fixture fail.
// Observed: Trace([0:42]) in the node-walk and the JIT: the fold's callback
//   `|acc, x| x + 1` never reads acc, so the fold yields 42 with an init that
//   is bottom (this file, f's base arm divides by zero) or never arrives
//   (`never<i64>()` gives 42 too), exactly the value the fixture asserts.
{
  let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n { i64:0 => i64:1 / i64:0, _ => n + f(n - i64:1) };
  any(array::fold([i64:41], f(i64:256), |acc, x| x + i64:1), i64:-1)
}
